ubuntu-gaming-mode (2.8.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an optional Debconf choice to install and select the UGM-ICONS theme
    for the configured desktop user, preserving existing icon files and
    restoring the prior selection only when UGM still owns the choice.
  * Bundle the user-provided theme in the package and align runtime identity
    with 2.8.2-1.

 -- N3ruk <csz_11@hotmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200

ubuntu-gaming-mode (2.8.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run the official Decky installer with umask 022, isolated from private
    UGM state permissions; ensure PluginLoader is readable/executable by
    unprivileged plugin workers, including existing 2.8.0-1 installs.
  * Set explicit bundled plugin payload permissions and reload active Decky
    after plugin installation, preserving existing plugins and stopped services.
  * Align package, managed-state and Doctor/inventory versions with 2.8.0-2.

 -- N3ruk <csz_11@hotmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200

ubuntu-gaming-mode (2.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First local 2.8 package, not published.
  * Include Gamescope downsampling sharpener 0.4 (patch 0010).
  * Add independent opt-in Decky Loader and bundled filter plugins.
  * Add per-controller USB wake policy for Bluetooth wake installations.
  * Integrate audited shared AMD/NVIDIA VRS layers for 32/64 bits,
    conservative shader policy, GPL support and lower CPU allocation cost.
  * Align Doctor runtime identity and inventory cache with 2.8.0-1;
    require root for private state checks instead of false missing-file errors.

 -- N3ruk <csz_11@hotmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

ubuntu-gaming-mode (2.5.0-5) unstable; urgency=low

  * Retain the validated Gamescope 3.16.30 GBM runtime and nine-patch source.
  * Add GPU/Vulkan inventory, HDR/VRR preferences and capability diagnostics.
  * Bundle native RADV VRS support and opt-in AMD/NVIDIA Vulkan VRS layers
    built for 32- and 64-bit applications.
  * Stage selected VRS layers from the readable package payload, keeping
    private installation state inaccessible to the Steam session.
  * Bundle the optional Bluetooth controller-wake app, icon, Polkit policy and
    service; recommend BlueZ and keep the option disabled by default.

 -- N3ruk <csz_11@hotmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200

ubuntu-gaming-mode (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the reproducible Gamescope 3.16.30 GBM runtime and nine-patch source record.
  * Add the optional console-style physical power-button integration.
  * Add an optional reversible /usr/local/bin/gamescope link to UGM's runtime.
  * Preserve Desktop power-button handling outside managed Gaming Mode.
  * Extend diagnostics, rollback and clean-install validation for 2.0.0.

